# Line endings are part of the contract for anything a shell or a CI runner
# executes, so they are pinned here rather than left to each developer's
# core.autocrlf setting.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true rewrites the shell
# scripts to CRLF and they stop running: bash reports `set: -: invalid option`
# on the first line and `$'\r': command not found` on every other. CI never
# sees it, because ubuntu-latest checks out LF, so the scripts look fine in
# every green build while being unusable for anyone cloning on Windows.

*.sh text eol=lf

# The CI entrypoints are parsed by GitHub's runner, not by a shell on the
# contributor's machine, but keeping them LF means a local run of the same
# commands sees the same bytes the runner will.
.github/workflows/*.yml text eol=lf

# Node scripts tolerate either ending, so they are left to the local setting.
# This is deliberate: pinning them would rewrite every .mjs file in the working
# tree for no functional gain.
